            <ArticleTitle>Cobalt-catalyzed aryl C-H activation and highly regioselective intermolecular annulation of sulfonamides with allenes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1872-1875</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc08622e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herein we describe a cobalt-catalyzed C-H activation of aryl and heteroaryl sulfonamides and their intermolecular heteroannulation reaction with allenes, providing a convergent strategy for the synthesis of biologically interesting heterocyclic scaffolds. Carbometallation of allenes proceeds selectively through a Co-alkenyl pathway for a wide range of electron-poor and electron-rich allenes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
